Subject: Card names: one front-face rule for every collection lookup

Scryfall's POST /cards/collection finds a split, adventure, modal
double-faced or transform card by its front face only: {"name": "Fire"}
returns Fire // Ice, {"name": "Fire // Ice"} is not_found (checked
2026-10-28). scryfall_card_text, scryfall_price_list and format_archidekt
sent the full name and reported "Fire // Ice" and "Brazen Borrower // Petty
Theft" as not found. validate_decklist indexed what came back by the full
name ("fire // ice") and looked cards up by the name given, so "Fire",
"Fire // Ice" and "Wear // Tear" in a Galadriel deck were neither flagged
outside the commander's colors nor reported missing: a card that could not
be matched was skipped without a word.

This patch adds one rule, _collection_name (the front face of "A // B"),
used by every name identifier: the decklist entries (card text, price
list), format_archidekt, validate_decklist, validate_archidekt_deck,
precon_diff's names, the goldfish card fetch and the watchlist bulk add.
_collection_lookup asks for names 75 at a time and matches each card back
under its full name or any face (_card_name_aliases), falling back to
Scryfall's identifier order. validate_decklist and validate_archidekt_deck
list every card a failed request could not check ("could not be checked")
instead of passing it, and check color identity by the names given.
scryfall_card_text's not-found lines name what the user wrote.

Tests: tests/test_card_face_names.py (a split, an adventure, a transform
and a modal double-faced card, by full name and by front face).

Upstream: Kautiontape/mystic-forge at dd82cd1 has no fix. Needs patches
0001-0012 applied first.

